{"id": "269437", "name": "נגזרות חלקיות קיימות והפונקציה לא רציפה – xy/(x²+3y²) (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"> </p>\n<p>Let \\( f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{cc}{{CT:0}} &amp; (x,y)\\neq (0,0) \\\\0 &amp; (x,y)=(0,0)\\end{array}\\right. \\)</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"><span> </span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"><span>The graph of \\(f(x,y)\\)</span>:</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"><img src=\"data/269437/files/1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"316\" /><br /><strong>Calcuate the partial derivatives of \\(f(x,y)\\) and their value at \\((0,0)\\): </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\">(For infinity write <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">inf</span>, for minus infinity write <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">minf</span> and for not defined write <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">nd</span>)</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Remark</span>: The answer will be Printed as the program interprets it, please verify it's as expected.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\">\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((x,y)\\)=[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"> </p>\n<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((x,y)\\)=[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((0,0)\\)=[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((0,0)\\)=[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Is \\(f(x,y)\\) continuous on \\(R^2\\)? [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>", "generalfeedback": "", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br />[[feedback:prt2]]<br />[[feedback:prt3]]<br />[[feedback:prt4]]<br />[[feedback:prt5]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 25, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 25, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans4", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans5", "type": "boolean", "boxsize": 10, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 2, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "fx", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is correct.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is incorrect.</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "fy", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is correct.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is incorrect.</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<p>Correct answer, \\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((0,0)=0\\)</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<p>Inorrect answer. By definition</p>\n<p> \\( \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\( (0,0)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(h,0)-f(0,0)}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{h \\cdot0}{h^2}=0 \\)</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt4", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans4", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt4-1-T", "feedback": "<p>Correct answer, \\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((0,0)=0\\)</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt4-1-F", "feedback": "<p> </p>\n<p>Inorrect answer. By definition</p>\n<p> \\( \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\( (0,0)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(0,h)-f(0,0)}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{0 \\cdot h}{3h^2}=0 \\)</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt5", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans5", "tans": "false", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt5-1-T", "feedback": "<p>Well done! Indeed \\(f(x,y)\\) isn't continuous at \\((0,0)\\).</p>\n<p>By taking the path \\((t,t)\\) when \\(t→0\\) we get</p>\n<p>\\( \\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{ t\\cdot t}{t^2+3t^2}=\\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}\\neq f(0,0) \\)</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Notice, </strong>\\(f(x,y)\\) is an example for a function which has both partial derivatives at \\((0,0)\\) and they are equal, but \\(f(x,y)\\) iself isn't coninuous.</p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>\n<p> </p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt5-1-F", "feedback": "<p>Incorrect answer! Note that \\(f(x,y)\\) isn't continuous at \\((0,0)\\) </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>By taking the path \\((t,t)\\) when \\(t→0\\) we get</p>\n<p>\\( \\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{ t\\cdot t}{t^2+3t^2}=\\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}\\neq f(0,0) \\)</p>\n<p><strong>Notice, </strong>\\(f(x,y)\\) is an example for a function which has both partial derivatives at \\((0,0)\\) and they are equal, but \\(f(x,y)\\) iself isn't coninuous.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["f", "fx", "fy"], "nvariants": 1}